      "writtenOn": "2021-08-23T05:37:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Okay, it makes sense. However, if we want to remove such context switches, we really need to do one of the followings:\n\n1) A guest VM makes three connections with the virtualization service: VirtualMachineService, stdout, stderr. I think this is against our decision.\n2) The RPC vsock connection supports passing a file descriptor, which is not supported yet.\n3) We give up handling payload outputs. (Seems like a bad idea though!)\n4) Each payload opens its own output server. This would be fine, but we still need context switches within the app, because we don\u0027t wait for the connection to output server forever.\n\nWill there be any better ideas?",
